The surface fence, NVK's half. NullMoth's own change (not an upstream Mesa commit).
NVRM.kext keeps, per IOSurface, the holds of the command buffers still drawing into it and reads their completion
from the writing channel's own semaphore page (user client selector 12). This patch registers each channel with the
kernel and deletes it before its pages are freed, publishes the value of each flush beside the completion value,
exports nvmtl_nvk_fence_v1 for the Metal plugin (QUERY, OPEN, ARM, CLOSE, WAIT), lets a wait on a channel without
an event sleep in the kernel on that channel's semaphore, and provides the call that re-points a rebuilt channel.
The numbers and structs are in nvkmd/nvrm/nvrm_fence_abi.h, a byte-for-byte copy of kexts/NVRM/nvrm_fence_abi.h
(tools/test_shared_headers.py compares them; tools/test_fence_wiring_nvk.py holds the wiring).
A kext without the fence, or booted with nvrmfence=0, leaves every process on the 2.9 surface marks.

